 },
 "parts": [
  "Iff you're under thirty-one, you haven't lived a billion seconds yet.",
  "A million seconds is just under twelve days.",
  "So how long is a billion?",
  "That's almost thirty-two years.",
  "Here's the math.",
  "There are eighty-six thousand, four hundred seconds in a day.",
  "Divide a billion by that.",
  "Eleven thousand, five hundred seventy-four days.",
  "An average American life is only about two and a half billion seconds.",
  "Now try dollars.",
  "Spend one dollar every second.",
  "A million dollars is gone in under twelve days.",
  "A billion dollars lasts nearly thirty-two years.",
  "A million and a billion sound like neighbors. They're about thirty-two years apart.",
  "Now a trillion. That's a thousand billions.",
  "A trillion seconds is about thirty-one thousand, seven hundred years.",
  "A trillion seconds ago, it was the Ice Age.",
  "Woolly mammoths were alive.",
  "That's more than five times longer than writing has existed.",
  "A million is days.",
  "A billion is a lifetime.",
  "A trillion is the Ice Age.",
  "So how big is a trillion dollars?"
 ],
